# WP-029 — Independent Acceptance Criteria

Implementation actor is **not authorized to accept this package**.  
Independent verifier: **Specification Integrity Verifier**.

## Binary criteria

- [ ] **AC-01.** Purpose is demonstrated, not merely configured: Convert sealed AETHRION planning artifacts into a compact executable packet mechanically, not by model summarization.
- [ ] **AC-02.** Every mandatory deliverable exists, is non-empty and resolves to the candidate under review.
- [ ] **AC-03.** All mandatory core and package-specific adversarial tests PASS on the same candidate revision.
- [ ] **AC-04.** No Critical or High blocking finding remains.
- [ ] **AC-05.** No protected AETHRION_SPEC/frozen acceptance artifact was changed to obtain a pass.
- [ ] **AC-06.** Upstream revisions, license/provenance and effective runtime/model identities used by this package are recorded.
- [ ] **AC-07.** Required rollback/recovery/disable behavior was exercised rather than only documented.
- [ ] **AC-08.** Independent verifier can reproduce the verdict without producer conversation history.
- [ ] **AC-09.** Scope behavior holds: Read WP card/tests/acceptance companions.
- [ ] **AC-10.** Scope behavior holds: Resolve dependency outputs and linked ADRs/schemas/scenarios/reuse records.
- [ ] **AC-11.** Scope behavior holds: Capture frozen revision/hashes.
- [ ] **AC-12.** Scope behavior holds: Extract protected paths, non-waivable rules, required skills and evidence obligations.
- [ ] **AC-13.** Scope behavior holds: Produce template-free machine/human projections.
- [ ] **AC-14.** Scope behavior holds: Fail closed on missing/contradictory references.

## Automatic rejection/block conditions

- hard dependency not actually ACCEPTED;
- mandatory test skipped;
- evidence references a different candidate;
- implementation weakened its own acceptance/spec;
- safety/authority boundary exists only as prompt wording while capability remains available;
- unresolved license/provenance for a required upstream/model artifact;
- verifier lacks required independence;
- rollback/recovery required by this package cannot be safely exercised.

## Required acceptance packet

1. candidate revision/digest;
2. completed test record;
3. mandatory deliverables;
4. upstream lock entries;
5. environment manifest;
6. findings and dispositions;
7. rollback/recovery evidence;
8. verifier binding;
9. explicit `ACCEPTED | REJECTED | BLOCKED` verdict.

Acceptance proves this bounded capability only. It does not prove DUM-E v0.1 or full AETHRION commissioning readiness.
